          {
            title: 'Carpet',
            subtitle: 'Card Game',
            content: [
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: "Carpet is a simple and rewarding patience (solitaire) game. Four Aces form the foundations, twenty cards are laid out in a 5Ã—4 grid called the 'carpet,' and the remaining cards form a stock. The goal is to build all cards onto the foundations in suit from Ace to King.",
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: "Carpet is a traditional patience game of unknown origin. It belongs to the 'Calculation' family of solitaire games. The name comes from the 5Ã—4 grid of cards resembling a carpet pattern.",
              },
            ],
          },
          {
            title: 'Setup',
            subtitle: 'Table, deck, equipment, and deal',
            content: [
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: '1 player (solitaire)',
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: 'Standard 52-card pack. Remove the four Aces to form foundations. The remaining 48 cards are shuffled.',
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: 'Standard deck of cards, playing surface',
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: "Remove four Aces and place them as foundations. Deal 20 cards face up in a 5Ã—4 grid (the 'carpet') with no overlaps. Remaining 28 cards form the stock (held in hand). Discard pile starts empty.",
              },
            ],
          },
        ],
      },
